# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CCEX .gitignore
#
# Principle: ignore build artifacts only.
#
# test/code_verification/check_numerics/reference/ is tracked on purpose: the recorded
# files are the reference outputs used to check whether an optimization changes the
# numbers, .process logs included. test/code_verification/bath_data/ holds the inputs
# the rotation, input-form and pcce checks read.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- build artifacts --------------------------------------------------------
/bin/
/obj/
/obj_gpu/
# CMake builds (cmake -B build); the binaries still go to bin/
/build/
/build-*/
*.o
*.d

# The top-level Makefile is GENERATED: do_compile.sh writes it fresh for whichever
# server it is given, so it is never the same file on two machines. While it was
# tracked, every checkout sat permanently at " M Makefile" and any branch that
# happened to touch it made `git pull` refuse to run on every other machine.
#
# Run `bash do_compile.sh <idm4|idm3|nurion|mac|wsl>` before the first build; plain
# `make` in a fresh clone now fails loudly instead of quietly building with whatever
# flags the last committed version happened to carry.
#
/Makefile
/.ccex_makefile.stamp

# NOTE: do NOT add a global `*.out` rule. This repo tracks 60+ legitimate .out
#       files (DFT outputs under example/tutorial/08_hBN_VB_natab/bath/, QE outputs under
#       example/tools/SpinTensorReader/). The only build .out is bin/main.out, which
#       /bin/ above already covers.

# --- python caches ----------------------------------------------------------
# NOTE: many __pycache__/*.pyc are already tracked in this repo, so this rule
#       only stops NEW ones. To stop the tracked ones from showing up as
#       modified after every analyzer run, they must be untracked separately:
#           git rm --cached -r '**/__pycache__'
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- editor / OS ------------------------------------------------------------
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store

# --- run byproducts ---------------------------------------------------------
# Stray .process files from running the examples are noise, but the regression
# ones are reference data -- keep those.
*.process
!test/code_verification/check_numerics/**/*.process

# refinement port test build artifacts
test/cluster_verification/check_adaptive/cpp/bin*/
test/cluster_verification/check_adaptive/cpp/out/
test/cluster_verification/check_adaptive/cpp/*.gcov

# --- raw results ------------------------------------------------------------
# Server results, tarballs and SQLite caches under test/ belong in the archive
# (see docs/repository-consolidation-todo-20260922.md), not in git.
test/**/*.tar.gz
test/**/*.sqlite

# --- tutorial outputs -------------------------------------------------------
# A tutorial run writes results/, summary*/ and rawdata/ next to its input, plus
# logs and figures. The recorded ones went to the archive on 2026-09-23; new ones
# are not tracked.
example/tutorial/**/results/
example/tutorial/**/summary*/
example/tutorial/**/rawdata/
example/tutorial/**/*_noDiv
example/tutorial/**/*_wiDiv
example/tutorial/**/*_ErrCorr
example/tutorial/**/*EnsAvg*
example/tutorial/**/*.png
example/tutorial/**/outfile
example/tutorial/**/process*
example/tutorial/**/Process_*
example/tutorial/**/proc[0-9]*
example/tutorial/**/Submitted

# --- Doxygen output: docs/doxygen/do_doxy makes it -------------------------
docs/doxygen/html/
docs/doxygen/latex/
docs/doxygen/xml/
test/code_verification/check_numerics/_work/
test/code_verification/check_mean_field/_work/
test/code_verification/check_rdip_ladder/_work/
test/code_verification/check_master_equation/_work/
.vscode/

# per-folder run locks of the standing checks (D29)
**/.run.lock
example/tools/AutoConvergence/examples/nv13c/data/
example/tools/AutoConvergence/examples/nv13c/auto*/
